# UI Library Policy

- Use a wrapper-first architecture under `components/ui`, exported through `components/ui/index.ts`.
- Prefer Radix primitives as the headless foundation when needed.
- Keep component APIs consistent, simple, and project-owned.
- Avoid generator or copied patterns (including the shadcn CLI) that reduce clarity or increase churn.
- Prioritize accessibility defaults (focus, keyboard, semantic roles).
- Use shared utilities (`cn`) and design tokens for styling consistency.
- Validate new components with a section in the Components showcase (`app/components/sections`) before wider use. The `add-ui-component` skill covers the full flow.
